<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Selge</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 25 BCE (approx.) · capital Selge</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Selge, a powerful Pisidian mountain city in the Taurus, which claimed Spartan origins and fielded armies of thousands.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Selge was founded in the high <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamphylia">Pamphylia</a>, above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurymedon-river">Eurymedon</a> gorge. Its citizens claimed descent from Spartans and from the seer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calchas">Calchas</a>, but the city grew from a Pisidian community that became increasingly Greek from the 5th century BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Selge was a self-governing city controlling fertile upland valleys that produced olives, wine and storax resin used in perfume. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> says it could once field 20,000 men, and in 218 BCE it resisted a siege by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaeus-general">Achaeus</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Selge kept its independence until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> organised the region. In 25 BCE it became part of the province of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/galatia">Galatia</a> and lived on as a Roman provincial town.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/selge.jpg" alt="Selge" width="320" height="239"><figcaption>Image: Volker Höhfeld · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Selge_08_04_2015_Theater_von_Selge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 25 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Selge</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek and Pisidian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek, Pisidian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-212&amp;focus=selge" aria-label="Selge on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5459 837 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Selge lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5779 1093L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5779 1093h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5779 1093h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-212&amp;focus=selge">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

